# Snapshot of the kernel actually running on the i5-4590, captured with
# `make savedefconfig` from ~/kernel/linux-6.18.46 on 2026-08-28.
#
# This file is a RECORD, not build input. `make kernel` builds from upstream
# defconfig plus KERNEL_CONFIG_ENABLE in the Makefile; nothing reads this.
# It exists for two reasons:
#
#   - The running kernel was built by hand, outside the Docker build, and had
#     drifted. Eight options existed only in that build tree, including
#     SND_HDA_CODEC_HDMI, without which an ISO has no HDMI audio. The drift
#     was found by diffing this against the Makefile's list, which is only
#     possible if a copy like this exists.
#
#   - Trimming the kernel means removing drivers for hardware that is not
#     here -- 1,708 options are built in and the machine is one Haswell
#     desktop. This is the "before" to diff every removal against.
#
# savedefconfig lists only what differs from the architecture's defaults, so
# 5,324 lines of .config reduce to the few hundred below that were chosen.
#
